  "answer": "This has been reported before (PowerToys#46992): PuTTY's custom system menu disappears for PuTTY windows launched while PowerToys is running. A commenter on that ticket traced it to the Always On Top module, which added a 'Toggle always on top' entry to the window system menu. Disabling the Always On Top module in PowerToys Settings makes the problem go away. Turning off the 'Show Always on Top in the title bar context menu' option or adding putty.exe to the Excluded apps list did not help. Launching PuTTY as administrator also avoids it. Another commenter pointed to #46569 as a possible duplicate. That ticket was not among those shown to me, so I can't confirm it. No fix is recorded in the tickets I was shown, so disable Always On Top for now and follow #46992 for a fix. Reinstalling will not change this."
 },
